  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "libgsasl security update",
      "Title": "Synopsis",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libgsasl is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4",
      "Title": "Summary",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "The library includes support for the SASL framework and at least partial support for the CRAM-MD5, EXTERNAL, GSSAPI, ANONYMOUS, PLAIN, SECURID, DIGEST-MD5, LOGIN, and NTLM mechanisms.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nIn GNU SASL before 2.2.3, DIGEST-MD5 has a NULL pointer dereference affecting both clients and servers, via a known token with no accompanying = character. This occurs in lib/digest-md5/getsubopt.c.(CVE-2026-48829)\n\nGNU SASL before 2.2.4 lacks sanitization of a short challenge in _gsasl_ntlm_client_step in the NTLM client, which could result in memory disclosure via a crafted server.(CVE-2026-56968)",
      "Title": "Description",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "An update for libgsasl is now available for openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4.\n\nopenEuler Security has rated this update as having a security impact of high. A Common Vunlnerability Scoring System(CVSS)base score,which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVElink(s) in the References section.",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "High",
      "Title": "Severity",
      "Type": "General"
    },
    {
      "Text": "libgsasl",
      "Title": "Affected Component",
      "Type": "General"
    }
  ],
